0,Music of the Democratic Republic of the Congo - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_the_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo,"June 1, 2026 - Congolese popular music developed alongside the urban growth of Léopoldville (now Kinshasa) in the 1930s and the expansion of colonial commercial enterprises, which exposed local musicians to global genres such as Cuban rumba, jazz, blues, biguine, highlife, and bolero.",Khe,Niger-Congo
